WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
6: Describing People and Things.

2
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:10.140
Here you learn how to describe
people and things with precise words.

3
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.660
You collect words for what somebody is like
inside, such as kind, honest, friendly and careless,

4
00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:22.440
and words for what things are like outside,
such as rough, tough, similar and alive.

5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.400
You compare two people with kinder and busier,
you tell true stories in the past simple,

6
00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.360
and you use could to say what somebody was able to do.

7
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:38.600
Along the way you read about Amal, a new girl who discovers
that carrying kindness makes everybody feel welcome.

8
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.280
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

9
00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:51.500
By the end of this unit, you will be able to use describing
words (adjectives) to talk about people and things.

10
00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:56.080
You will also describe your favourite
person and say what makes them special.

11
00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:01.220
You will also compare two people or things,
using words like kinder and rougher than.

12
00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.780
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:11.840
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
clear, fear, deer, especially, possibly, certainly.

14
00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:17.760
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:22.420
The reading sequence includes My Cousin Noah and Two Roads.

16
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:28.120
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

17
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.140
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

18
00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:36.440
The first language focus is The Past Simple Tense.

19
00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.180
We use the past simple to talk
about things that already happened.

20
00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:46.340
It helps us tell stories and describe what people
did, like Nora, who helped the boy who fell.

21
00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:50.400
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:55.560
In speaking, you will complete Speaking
1 — Describe Your Favourite Person.

23
00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:58.940
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:06.300
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:08.420
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:14.860
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:21.780
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
